Feature: every file bootstrap-tools writes into bootstrap says so, and names bootstrap-tools as the writer

  Background:
    Given bootstrap checked out beside the tools

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::generatedKindNamesWriter
  Scenario Outline: <kind> (<files>)
    Given the <kind> found on disk: <files>
    Then there is at least one such file
    And every one of them contains the generated-by notice

    Examples:
      | kind | files |
      | published JSON Schemas | every bootstrap/schemas/*.schema.json |
      | the drawn schema page | schemas/README.md |
      | the vocabulary | ns.jsonld |
      | each Process's picture | every bootstrap/processes/*.svg |

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::vocabularyAttributedInRdf
  Scenario: the vocabulary also says it in RDF: prov:wasAttributedTo the tools repository
    Then bootstrap/ns.jsonld's wasAttributedTo is the tools repository address

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::authoredFileNotClaimed
  Scenario: an AUTHORED file does not claim to be generated
    Given every .bpmn in bootstrap/processes and bootstrap.json
    Then none contains the generated-by notice

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::partlyGeneratedClaimsRegions
  Scenario: a PARTLY generated README claims only its marker regions, and every region says so at its top
    Given bootstrap/README.md
    Then it has at least one begin/end marker region
    And every region's body starts with the generated-by notice
    And the text outside the regions does not contain the notice
    And the file is not read as wholly generated

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::directoryReadmeOpensWithNotice
  Scenario: every directory README opens with the notice, linking bootstrap-tools
    Given the README.md of each non-hidden directory of bootstrap that has one
    Then there is at least one
    And each, in its first three lines after any front matter, says the page was generated by bootstrap-tools, linking the tools repository
    And each is read as wholly generated

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::noticeNamesAndLinksScript
  Scenario: names the script, links it, and reads back
    When a section banner is generated for "scripts/x.ts", from "the `a` entry (of b)", saying instead "change it"
    Then it links `scripts/x.ts` to that script in the tools repository
    And it says "This section was generated by"
    And reading it back yields that one script, its from and its instead

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::frontMatterIsOneKey
  Scenario: is one `generated:` key, read back as this script's own
    Given the generated front matter for "scripts/x.ts"
    Then its YAML is a "generated:" key naming scripts/x.ts of the bootstrap toolset with its address
    And it is read back as scripts/x.ts's own front matter on a page that starts with it
    And it is not read back as scripts/y.ts's own
    And it is not read back when it is merged into front matter that also holds a title

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::frontMatterIsNotSecondNote
  Scenario: is not a second note: the notes still count one per banner
    Given the generated front matter followed by one banner
    Then reading the notes back yields exactly 1

  @test:scripts/generated-by.test.ts::frontMatterKeepsGeneratedPage
  Scenario: does not make a wholly generated page look authored
    Given a page of the generated front matter followed by one marker region holding a banner
    Then it is read as wholly generated
